From: Dean Marx <dean.marx@canonical.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:28:36 +0900
Subject: network/route: preserve IPv4 route MTU (LP: #2167098)

In systemd v250, commit 3b6a3bdebfb ("network: use
NetworkConfigSource/State to manage addresses and routes") changed how
networkd handles route requests. Before that commit, link_request_route()
queued each newly requested Route object, which was then passed to
route_configure(), which built and sent an RTM_NEWROUTE rtnetlink message
to the kernel. The kernel then decided whether the message described a new
route or an update to an existing route, based on the kernel routing key.

After 3b6a3bdebfb, link_request_route() first calls route_get() to check
whether networkd is already tracking an equivalent Route object. If a
match is found, networkd reuses the previously tracked object instead of
the newly requested one, copying only a few select fields such as
source, provider, and later lifetime_usec. The problem is that this match
is decided by route_hash_func() and route_compare_func(), and in v255
those functions do not include Route.mtu. As a result, a route request
that differs only in MTU is treated as matching the existing tracked
route. The newly requested object, carrying the updated MTU, is discarded,
and the stale tracked object is passed to route_configure() instead.

route_configure() already knows how to send Route.mtu to the kernel as
RTAX_MTU inside the RTA_METRICS container. The bug is that, after the
v250 route request refactor, route_configure() can be given the stale
tracked Route object rather than the freshly requested one. This causes
the old MTU to be sent back to the kernel and the updated MTU to be lost.

This patch is a targeted v255 fix for that behaviour. It includes
Route.mtu in the IPv4 route hash and comparison functions, so two IPv4
routes that differ only in MTU are no longer treated as the same tracked
route. It also reads RTAX_MTU from received rtnetlink route messages into
Route.mtu, so Route objects built from kernel notifications have the same
MTU information that networkd sends during route configuration.

Upstream no longer has this bug in v256 and later, but the upstream fix
is not a single small change that can be applied directly to v255. Commit
d32a520b095f ("network/route-metric: introduce RouteMetric") moved route
metric fields, including MTU, out of struct Route and into struct
RouteMetric. Commit ebf4fa1e82b ("network/route-metric: manage uint32_t
RTAX_XYZ attributes in the same way") then stored those values in a
RouteMetric.metrics array indexed by RTAX_* attributes. This made MTU
available as metrics[RTAX_MTU], and route_metric_compare_func() compares
that metrics array as a whole. Commit 7027cdbd79c ("network/route:
remove existing route if some property conflict with requested ones")
then added route_can_update() / route_metric_can_update(), so networkd
can reject reuse of an existing route whose metrics do not match the
requested route.

Backporting that upstream implementation would require bringing in the
larger RouteMetric refactoring and its dependent changes. Instead, this
vendor patch reproduces the relevant behaviour using the v255 data
structure: MTU remains stored in Route.mtu, but it is now a part of
the same route identity decision that determines whether an existing
tracked route may be reused.

Origin: vendor
Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167098
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-22
---
 src/network/networkd-route.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/network/networkd-route.c b/src/network/networkd-route.c
index b7de582..189402c 100644
--- a/src/network/networkd-route.c
+++ b/src/network/networkd-route.c
@@ -141,6 +141,9 @@ static void route_hash_func(const Route *route, struct siphash *state) {
                 siphash24_compress(&route->scope, sizeof(route->scope), state);
                 siphash24_compress(&route->type, sizeof(route->type), state);
 
+                if (route->family == AF_INET)
+                        siphash24_compress(&route->mtu, sizeof(route->mtu), state);
+
                 siphash24_compress(&route->initcwnd, sizeof(route->initcwnd), state);
                 siphash24_compress(&route->initrwnd, sizeof(route->initrwnd), state);
 
@@ -222,6 +225,12 @@ static int route_compare_func(const Route *a, const Route *b) {
                 if (r != 0)
                         return r;
 
+                if (a->family == AF_INET) {
+                        r = CMP(a->mtu, b->mtu);
+                        if (r != 0)
+                                return r;
+                }
+
                 r = CMP(a->initcwnd, b->initcwnd);
                 if (r != 0)
                         return r;
@@ -1870,6 +1879,12 @@ int manager_rtnl_process_route(sd_netlink *rtnl, sd_netlink_message *message, Ma
                 return 0;
         }
         if (r >= 0) {
+                r = sd_netlink_message_read_u32(message, RTAX_MTU, &tmp->mtu);
+                if (r < 0 && r != -ENODATA) {
+                        log_link_warning_errno(link, r, "rtnl: received route message with invalid MTU, ignoring: %m");
+                        return 0;
+                }
+
                 r = sd_netlink_message_read_u32(message, RTAX_INITCWND, &tmp->initcwnd);
                 if (r < 0 && r != -ENODATA) {
                         log_link_warning_errno(link, r, "rtnl: received route message with invalid initcwnd, ignoring: %m");
